Description: Fix GCC 15 libstdc++ std::optional::emplace() with aggregate types
 GCC 15's libstdc++ std::optional::emplace() requires is_constructible_v<T>
 to be satisfied. C++20 aggregates with default member initializers don't
 satisfy is_constructible_v in GCC 15's implementation, causing compilation
 errors. This patch replaces emplace() calls with direct aggregate
 initialization assignments, which works with both libc++ and libstdc++.
 .
 Files fixed:
 - mojo/public/cpp/bindings/lib/multiplex_router.cc
 - third_party/webrtc/call/rtp_config.cc
 - cc/tiles/gpu_image_decode_cache.cc
 - third_party/blink/renderer/core/paint/paint_layer_scrollable_area.h
 - third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/inline/line_breaker.cc
Author: Juan Manuel Mendez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-12-01

